{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be helping take care of you during your stay. I know you're here because of increased pain around your trach site and some chest discomfort. Can you tell me more about that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. The pain started yesterday. It’s right where the T-tube goes in. It hurts more when I swallow or move my neck. And my chest feels sore in the middle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, chills, or changes in your breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No fever. Breathing is okay, but I’ve been avoiding eating because it hurts too much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll get you some pain control. For now, we’re going to hold off on food and meds by mouth until ENT and pulmonology see you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. But I need my reflux meds. I get heartburn if I miss them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2166-09-06 20:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll give your omeprazole through your feeding tube if needed. Your safety comes first. We’ll restart your diet as soon as we know it’s safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2166-09-06 22:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The ENT team did a laryngoscopy. They didn’t see any infection or inflammation in your trachea. That’s good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2166-09-06 22:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not infected? Why does it hurt so much?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2166-09-06 22:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We don’t know yet. It could be irritation or granulation tissue. We’re ordering a CT scan of your trachea to look deeper."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2166-09-07 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT scan is back. There’s no sign of infection, fluid collection, or esophageal compression. The pain isn’t showing a clear cause on imaging."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2166-09-07 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s frustrating. So what now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2166-09-07 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We think it’s likely post-op pain from the T-tube site. We’ll restart your diet based on your last speech and swallow evaluation since they weren’t here yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2166-09-07 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember that — thin liquids and regular solids, right? With sips in between bites?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2166-09-07 09:37:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. And three times daily oral care. The speech team will see you later to confirm."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2166-09-07 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re starting IV morphine for your pain since your oral meds weren’t strong enough at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2166-09-07 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I was really struggling to eat because of the pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2166-09-07 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We also noticed you were a bit lightheaded on admission. That’s likely from not eating or drinking enough. We’re giving IV fluids and encouraging you to drink."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2166-09-07 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel less dizzy now. I had some apple juice and crackers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2166-09-07 12:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. That’s exactly what we wanted to see. Your oxygen levels have stayed stable too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2166-09-07 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The speech and swallow team saw you. They say your swallowing looks the same as before. You can keep your current diet."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2166-09-07 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried I’d have to go back to pureed food."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2166-09-07 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not this time. We’re also continuing your levofloxacin. It was started during your last admission for tracheitis prevention."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2166-09-07 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is there an infection now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2166-09-07 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of active infection. But we’re finishing the course as planned. Better safe than sorry."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2166-09-08 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your pain is doing better with the IV meds. We’d like to switch you to oral Percocet to see if that controls it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2166-09-08 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve used oxycodone before. Will that work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2166-09-08 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We checked your prescription history. You can use the oxycodone and liquid Tylenol you have at home for breakthrough pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2166-09-08 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The oral meds are helping. Pain is about a 3 now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2166-09-08 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. We’ll keep monitoring. Also, your labs show you have a long-standing mild anemia. It hasn’t changed. You should follow up with your doctor after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2166-09-08 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had that for years. Should I be worried?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2166-09-08 10:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s stable, so no emergency. But an outpatient workup is a good idea to understand the cause."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2166-09-08 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One more thing — your CT showed a small 7 mm spot in your liver. It’s unchanged from before, so likely not serious. But your PCP should follow it up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2166-09-08 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A liver spot? Is it cancer?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2166-09-08 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No signs of that. It’s stable, which is reassuring. But we always check these things over time. Your doctor will monitor it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Pain is controlled, you’re eating and drinking, and your breathing is stable. We think you’re ready to go home today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If your secretions increase, change color, or smell bad, or if you get fevers, worsening pain, or trouble breathing — come back right away."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Keep using your reflux meds, stay on your current diet, and finish your antibiotics. And follow up for your anemia and liver spot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thank you for helping me feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2166-09-09 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you only if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2166-09-06 20:07:00",
    "admission_end": "2166-09-09 17:14:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia, tracheostomy, and multiple airway reconstructions was admitted for increased trach site pain, chest discomfort, and reduced oral intake due to pain. She was initially managed with NPO status and IV pain control. ENT evaluation and CT trachea showed no infection, inflammation, or structural cause for pain. She resumed her prior diet after speech and swallow assessment confirmed safety. Pain was transitioned from IV morphine to oral oxycodone, with plans to continue home medications. Lightheadedness resolved with IV fluids and improved intake. Chronic microcytic anemia was noted and recommended for outpatient workup. A stable 7 mm liver hypodensity was identified on CT and communicated to her PCP. She improved clinically and was discharged home with instructions to monitor for worsening symptoms and complete follow-up for anemia and liver imaging.",
    "problems": [
      "Other acute postoperative pain",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Other anomalies of larynx, trachea, and bronchus",
      "Other chronic bronchitis",
      "Unspecified disorder of liver",
      "Dehydration",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Iron deficiency anemia, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
